<task id="145" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>ACTIVELY TRACKED (owner) — the Secure Record Owner role must hold the privileges every child re-own needs, in every environment: verify word-add-in-r1 task 082's grant, extend the ONE codified set to every table UAC-r2 re-owns, standing census clause, new-environment provisioning step</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (authored 2026-09-30, session 27; owner round 2 item 11; GitHub #1046)</phase>
    <gate>Steps 1-2 (tracking, census of tables) startable now. Steps 3-6 (live extension grant, census clause, pipeline) wait for word-add-in-r1 task 082 to land its codified JSON set, its script, its guide rows and its five-table grant (#1046) — or for the owner's decision under the first escalation trigger. Step 5 (census clause retarget) and the named-team verification wait for task 144 (the role's holder moves to 144's named team; 144 rewrites SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion clause 2).</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes a live Dataverse security role on the secure-isolation boundary; tags auth, security, dataverse; adds a standing check and a provisioning step.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Least-privilege security-role work on the isolation anchor: an over-grant recreates the hole the Secure Record BU exists to close, an under-grant makes every secure child write fail closed. Cross-project coordination with word-add-in-r1 task 082 on one shared live role.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion*.cs after task 144 (144 rewrites clause 2 in the same file), extends the codified set file owned by word-add-in-r1 task 082, and changes a live role shared with 082. Tasks 146, 148 and 149 depend on this one.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>144 (census clause + named-team verification); external: word-add-in-r1 task 082 / #1046 (codified set, script, guide rows, five-table grant)</deps>
    <tags>dataverse, auth, security, security-role, provisioning, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>5-8 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Owner round 2 item 11 (2026-09-30): "The Secure Record Owner role's missing child-table privileges must be ACTIVELY TRACKED as a UAC-r2 issue and task, not left in the peer's notes." Peer record: word-add-in-r1 note 080 §6.12, task 082, GitHub #1046, PR #1045. Agreed split recorded in session27 note "Peer follow-through".</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Dataverse refuses to make a team the owner of a row unless the team's role holds the required privilege on that row's table. The Secure Record Owner role covers only the root tables and sprk_document in dev (and only the three root tables in any environment built from the guide), so every child of a secure record that is re-owned to the secure team fails closed. Word-add-in-r1 task 082 grants the five tables its Office writers and the owner named need and builds the ONE codified set. This task makes sure that happens (it is the owner's tracker), extends the set to every other table UAC-r2's C10 part 2 re-owns, adds the standing census check, and makes every new environment end up with the same role.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer on the secure-record isolation boundary. Least-privilege discipline: every privilege added names the writer that needs it and is proven by a recorded refusal before and success after.</role>

  <goal>(1) Word-add-in-r1 task 082's grant (Read at User depth on sprk_document, sprk_todo, sprk_communication, sprk_event, sprk_memo) is verified live and recorded, or — if 082 has not landed — the owner has decided who applies it and it is applied once; (2) the ONE codified set (082's JSON data file) lists every child table that any UAC-r2 writer (task 146 census, 147 client-created children, 148 backfill/transitions) can assign to the secure team, each with its reason, and the live role holds Read at User depth on every one of them, and nothing beyond what a recorded failure forced; (3) the NFR-05 census has a clause that fails naming any table in the set the role lacks, reading the same file; (4) the role is held only by task 144's named owner team; (5) a new environment gets the Secure BU, the named owner team, the role and the full set through the provisioning pipeline or runbook step with no hand-edited list; (6) #1046 is closed once, citing both tasks.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>🔴 THIS GAP HAD TWO OWNERS AND THEREFORE NONE. Word-add-in-r1's note 080 §6.12 said "UAC-r2's C10 adds the child-table privileges"; UAC-r2's session-27 note said "fails closed until UAC C10 lands". The owner ruled 2026-09-30 that it is ACTIVELY TRACKED in UAC-r2 — this task. Word-add-in-r1 then filed GitHub #1046 and authored task 082 (branch work/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1, status not-started 2026-09-30), stating ownership moved to it "at the owner's instruction". The two sessions AGREED a split (session27 note, "Peer follow-through"; 082 background "Agreed with unified-access-control-r2"):
- 082: grants Read at User depth on sprk_todo, sprk_communication, sprk_event, sprk_memo (sprk_document already present in dev) on the EXISTING role; creates the ONE codified set as a machine-readable JSON DATA FILE (one entry per table: logical name, privilege name, the writer or owner decision that requires it) plus `scripts/Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1` (reads the file, derives ids from metadata, dry-run default, add-only, `-Verify`); edits guide §5.1 table and child-entities row, §5.3 `$securable`, §5.4 `$keep`, §7 check 1 to read or point to the file; puts the drift to the owner; does NOT edit `SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion*`.
- UAC-r2: owns `SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion*` (144 rewrites clause 2 for the named team; THIS task adds the "role lacks Read on a codified table" clause); extends the codified set to every table its C10 part-2 tasks re-own (tasks 146/147/148 treat this task as the owner of those privileges — 148's escalation: "the fix belongs in 145's codified set").
This task is UAC-r2's tracker for the whole gap: it verifies 082 rather than duplicating it, and does everything 082 does not.

THE PREMISE THE GUIDE STILL STATES IS FALSE. `docs/guides/SECURE-PROJECT-ENVIRONMENT-SETUP.md:161-168` grants `Read` at User depth on `sprk_project`, `sprk_matter` and `sprk_workassignment` only, and `:193` says "Anything on child entities — Nothing assigns children to this team. Granting here would be privilege without a purpose." Record-first ownership (`Services/Dataverse/RecordOwnershipResolver.cs:144-180`, wired for Office on PR #1045) and the C10 part-2 child re-own both assign children to the secure team. The guide's strip script keeps only the three root Reads (`:252`, `$keep`), and its §7 check 1 expects "exactly 3" (`:353`) — so re-running the documented procedure REMOVES whatever child privilege dev has. (082 fixes these rows; this task verifies they read the codified file.)

LIVE ROLE, measured by the peer 2026-09-30 (spaarkedev1, role e4ebabd9-b4a0-f111-aaac-000d3a99d1d7, 36 privileges): sprk_document all 8 at User; sprk_todo, sprk_communication, sprk_event, sprk_memo NONE; the three roots all 8 at User; the SharePoint four at Global. The drift is the 7 non-Read privileges on each of the 4 root and document tables (28) plus the SharePoint four — 082 puts it to the owner.

THE TABLE SET IS NOT JUST THE FIVE THE OWNER NAMED. design.md §5.1d (`design.md:552-603`) enumerates 18 business entities with a lookup to sprk_project (agreement, analysis, billingevent, budget, communication, communicationthread, document, event, externalrecordaccess, invoice, kpiassessment, memo, reportcard, servicerequest, spendsignal, spendsnapshot, todo, workassignment) plus `email`; sprk_matter and sprk_workassignment have their own child sets. The required set is exactly the set of tables that any writer can assign to the secure team — derived from the writers (task 146's census, 147, 148), not from this paragraph.

NEW ENVIRONMENTS. No provisioning code creates the Secure Record BU, the owner team or this role: grep of `src/server/services` for `Secure Record` returns nothing, and `SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md` does not mention it. Security roles ship in the Tier-1 base solution (`src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/SolutionImport/CanonicalSolutionCatalog.cs:44`), but a solution cannot create a role inside a child BU nor assign it to a team, and the guide requires the role to be created in the Secure BU (`SECURE-PROJECT-ENVIRONMENT-SETUP.md:213-215`). Neither 082 nor any other task puts this setup into the provisioning pipeline — this task does.</background>
