  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: every privilege added. Default is `Read` at User (Basic) depth. Any other access type (Append, AppendTo, Assign, …) or depth is added ONLY when a recorded Dataverse refusal names it for a real re-own of that table; the refusal text is recorded in the task note. Never Business Unit, Deep or Global depth (guide §5.1 and §8).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the table set. Each table in the codified set names the writer (file:line) or the C10 part-2 task that assigns rows of it to the secure team. A table with neither is not added. A writer that can assign a table not in the set is a defect this task fixes by adding the table.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the live role. Do NOT remove or narrow any existing privilege, including the drift (28 non-Read privileges on the root and document tables, and the SharePoint four). Removal is an owner decision — 082 asks it; if 082 has not, this task asks, with evidence and a recommendation. Never ask twice.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the role's holders. The role is held by exactly one principal — task 144's named owner team. Never a user, never another team, never the Secure BU default team; never add a broad role to the owner team (guide §5.1, §8). SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion clauses 2 and 3 stay green.</constraint>
    <constraint source="coordination">Scope: the codified set, the script and the guide rows. ONE set: word-add-in-r1 task 082's JSON data file. This task EXTENDS that file (adds entries) and applies it with 082's script; it never creates a second list, a second script, or a copy of the list inside a test, a doc or a handler. The guide §5.1/§5.3/§5.4/§7 rows are 082's; this task verifies they read the file and edits them only if 082 has not (see the first escalation trigger).</constraint>
    <constraint source="coordination">Scope: every live write. Before any live write, read 082's POML status in the word-add-in-r1 worktree and message the word-add-in-r1 session. If 082 has applied its grant, this task VERIFIES it against the codified set and adds only the remainder; it never re-applies or reverts 082's changes. Never race the peer on the shared role.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: codification mechanics. Privilege ids and names are derived from metadata (`EntityDefinitions(...)/Privileges`), never hard-coded GUIDs (guide §5.3 casing warning). The apply is dry-run by default, idempotent, add-only, and pins the environment URL explicitly (guide §2); auth by an explicit-URL `az` token — no new client secret (ADR-028 A4).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D-1 / ADR-002">Scope: enforcement. No Dataverse plugin. The standing check is the NFR-05 live assertion family run as a MANUAL gate — no Dataverse in CI. The census clause's evaluation logic is unit-tested with seeded census input (no Dataverse).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D-13">Scope: the new-environment step. It runs per customer environment against that environment's Secure BU and named team; it never assumes a shared app registration or a fixed role id.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: live probes. Every probe record created to prove a grant is deleted afterwards and the deletion recorded. Probes use existing records/test users in their current BU — no user relocation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added or changed. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration tests, no ctor null-check tests; keep the census tests at their KEEP path (tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl).</constraint>
  </constraints>

