  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">TRACKING: the task note records 082's status, #1046's state and the peer exchange at start and at close; if 082 had not landed when step 3 was due, the owner's decision under the first escalation trigger is recorded and followed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The codified set (ONE JSON file) lists every table any writer can assign to the secure team, each with its writer file:line or C10 part-2 task cited; it includes at least sprk_document, sprk_communication, sprk_memo, sprk_event and sprk_todo, and every table in task 146's census, 147's client-created children and 148's backfill scope. No second copy of the list exists anywhere (grep recorded).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">MANUAL LIVE GATE, NEGATIVE CONTROL: before the grant, a probe re-own of a row of each table this task adds to the secure owner team is REFUSED and the recorded message names the missing privilege. If one is not refused, the premise for that table is recorded as wrong and it is not added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">MANUAL LIVE GATE, POSITIVE: after the grant, the same probes succeed and read-back shows `owningteam` = the secure owner team, stable across 3 polls; 082's five tables are verified the same way (probe or recorded 082 evidence); probes deleted and the deletion recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every privilege added is at User (Basic) depth; any non-Read access type added cites the recorded refusal that forced it; every privilege present before the change is still present (before/after lists with count and diff in the note).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AUTHORIZATION: the role is held by exactly one principal, task 144's named owner team; no user and no other team (including the Secure BU default team) holds it; NFR-05 clauses 2 and 3 pass against dev (manual run, output recorded).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: the census clause FAILS naming the table when the census input lacks one table's required privilege (unit test with seeded input AND a recorded manual run), and passes with the full set.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Re-running the guide's procedure (§5.3 then §5.4) against a role holding the set removes nothing in the set; §5.1, §5.3, §5.4 and §7 all read or point to the codified file.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A new environment gets the Secure BU, the named owner team, the role and the full privilege set through the chosen provisioning step, with no hand-edited privilege list; the step's dry run writes nothing and a second apply changes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The drift decision was put to the owner exactly once (by 082 or by this task) with a recommendation and the answer is recorded; nothing was removed without it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">#1046 closed once, citing this task and word-add-in-r1 task 082; the peer was told the outcome.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: the negative controls, the positive probes, the census clause's two seeded directions and the existing NFR-05 clauses. Anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the note.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Owner round 2 item 11 (session27 note) — this task exists so the gap is tracked in UAC-r2 and not lost between projects; it stays open until the live role is verified in dev AND new environments get it. Related: defect C10 (session26 note), task 144 (named owner team — the role's holder; rewrites clause 2), tasks 146/147/148 (child re-own; they define the table set and depend on this task), task 150 (FLS setup joins the same new-environment step), word-add-in-r1 task 082 and note 080 §6.12, PR #1045 (their Office secure saves and To Dos fail closed until the grant lands), #1034 (writers not yet on I-6). UPDATE 2026-09-30 (main session): 082 is LIVE in dev (role 36→40 privileges, +Read at Basic on todo/communication/event/memo; negative refusals captured before -Apply). Its codified set is `config/secure-record-owner-role.json` (schemaVersion 1; tables[].privilegeName, kind root|child, reason, evidence, addedBy; a howToExtend block) and `scripts/Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1 -Verify`, in word-add-in-r1 PR #1051 (docs+script+config). This task's census clause reads that file and asserts depth mask 1; 146 extends the set via howToExtend. The live census needs AZURE_TOKEN_CREDENTIALS=AzureCliCredential on a workstation (plain DefaultAzureCredential resolved only EnvironmentCredential) — document it in the runbook.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load all files in knowledge before starting. Coordinate with word-add-in-r1 before the first live write. Run alone: the live role is shared.</protocol>
    <outcome date="2026-10-01" branch="task/uac-r2-145">
